# Build context exclusions for the Layer 4 node image.
#
# BuildKit reads this file when the Dockerfile is not at the context root:
# it looks for `<dockerfile>.dockerignore` next to the Dockerfile. The
# context itself is the repository root, so without this the transfer
# carries a 5.5 GB virtualenv, a 1.6 GB git object store, and several
# agent-tooling caches — none of which a Rust build can use.
#
# The important consequence is not the size. It is that the Dockerfile
# can do a single `COPY . .` instead of enumerating every crate cargo
# has to resolve. Path dependencies, `[patch.crates-io]` overrides, and
# root-level leaf crates all escape `crates/`, and each one that gets
# forgotten fails the build during dependency resolution with an error
# that names a path rather than the mistake.
#
# SCOPE RULE, learned the hard way: only exclude what is provably
# irrelevant AND large. An earlier version of this file also excluded
# `cairo/`, which broke the build — `zk-circuit` reads
# `cairo/src/lib.cairo` at compile time. Prose directories total about
# 35 MB against a 7 GB context, so excluding them saves nothing and
# risks exactly that failure. Everything below is either a build output
# directory, a version-control store, a Python environment, or agent
# tooling state.

# Build output and the local toolchain cache. By far the largest
# source-tree-adjacent directory.
target/
**/target/

# Version control and CI. `.git` alone is 1.6 GB.
.git/
.github/
.gitignore

# Local virtualenvs and Python caches. `.venv` alone is 5.5 GB.
.venv/
venv/
**/__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# Agent tooling state and caches. Large, and none of it participates in
# a cargo build.
.claude/
.clinerules/
.agents/
agents/
.cocoindex_code/
.continue/
.cursor/
.gitnexus/
.jcode/
.mimocode/
.opencode/
.openclaude/
.playwright-mcp/

# Local test and analysis scratch output.
live-tests/
check_arc3b/
.octo/
.audit/
.audits/
tarpaulin-report.json
cobertura.xml
*.profraw

# NOT excluded, deliberately: `cairo/` (read by `zk-circuit` at compile
# time), `docs/`, `rfcs/`, `missions/`, `memory/`, `python/`,
# `examples/`, `packaging/`, `pipelines/`, and the root-level crates
# `determin/`, `octo-sync/`, `octo-transport/`, `quota-router/`,
# `quota-router-e2e-tests/`, `sync-e2e-tests/`. Several are read by
# build scripts; the rest are small.
#
# `crates/octo-cli/tests/` is also not excluded: the runtime stage
# copies `entrypoint.sh` out of the builder's filesystem, and that path
# has to be in the context for the copy to resolve.
